WEBVTT

00:03.718 --> 00:04.844
KATARA: Water...

00:04.928 --> 00:06.262
Earth...

00:06.346 --> 00:08.223
Fire...

00:08.306 --> 00:10.642
Air.

00:10.725 --> 00:12.018
Long ago...

00:12.101 --> 00:14.729
The four nations lived
together in harmony.

00:14.812 --> 00:19.067
Then everything changed
when the Fire Nation attacked.

00:19.150 --> 00:23.154
Only the Avatar, master of
all four elements, could stop them.

00:23.613 --> 00:25.198
But when the world
needed him most

00:25.281 --> 00:27.408
he vanished.

00:27.492 --> 00:30.828
A hundred years passed, and my brother
and I discovered the new Avatar...

00:30.912 --> 00:32.664
An airbender named Aang.

00:32.872 --> 00:35.208
And although his airbending
skills are great

00:35.291 --> 00:37.794
he has a lot to learn before
he's ready to save anyone.

00:37.877 --> 00:39.045
AANG: Oof.

00:39.170 --> 00:42.632
But I believe
Aang can save the world.

00:42.757 --> 00:44.175
( ♪... )

00:48.054 --> 00:50.306
( MAN READING )

00:50.473 --> 00:51.849
What about the invasion?

00:51.975 --> 00:54.394
We'll join up with my dad
and the invasion force

00:54.477 --> 00:56.145
on the day of the eclipse.

00:56.271 --> 00:58.189
SOKKA: Keep quiet.

00:58.314 --> 01:01.109
We're in enemy territory.

01:01.234 --> 01:04.279
KATARA: What we need is some
new clothes.

01:04.404 --> 01:06.322
AANG: Yeah, blending in
is better than hiding out.

01:06.447 --> 01:08.324
If we get Fire Nation disguises

01:08.449 --> 01:11.160
we'll be just as safe
as we would be hiding in a cave.

01:11.286 --> 01:13.371
Ta-da,
normal kid.

01:14.455 --> 01:15.456
KATARA: How do I look?

01:21.045 --> 01:25.133
( ♪... )

01:29.220 --> 01:30.722
( APPA GRUNTING )

01:30.847 --> 01:32.223
Momo?

01:32.348 --> 01:33.891
( MOMO CHATTERING )

01:34.017 --> 01:37.145
Oh, Momo?

01:37.270 --> 01:39.314
Ah. ( LAUGHS )

01:39.439 --> 01:43.151
You found me, buddy.

01:43.276 --> 01:45.403
Hey, guys, I think
this river's polluted.

01:45.528 --> 01:47.155
( INHALES, GRUNTS )

01:47.280 --> 01:50.867
( ALL GROANING )

01:50.992 --> 01:54.704
( SPITS )

01:54.829 --> 01:58.082
Well, that explains why I can't
catch a fish around here.

01:58.166 --> 02:02.211
Because normally my fishing
skills are... Off the hook.

02:02.295 --> 02:04.464
Get it,
like a fishing hook?

02:04.672 --> 02:07.050
Too bad your skills aren't
on the hook.

02:07.175 --> 02:11.346
( ALL LAUGHING )

02:11.471 --> 02:15.058
It looks like we'll need to go
somewhere else to get food.

02:15.141 --> 02:17.977
Assuming that'll fit into
Sokka's master schedule.

02:18.144 --> 02:20.313
Hm... It's doable.

02:20.438 --> 02:22.690
But that means only two
potty breaks today.

02:22.815 --> 02:25.234
Hey, maybe we can
get food there.

02:30.198 --> 02:32.700
Now you look just like
a little hill with horns.

02:32.825 --> 02:34.285
Bye, buddy.

02:34.410 --> 02:37.705
( APPA SNORTS, MOMO CHATTERS )

02:37.830 --> 02:40.083
TOPH: I don't feel anything.

02:40.208 --> 02:41.626
Where's this village?

02:41.751 --> 02:43.336
It's in the middle
of the river.

02:43.461 --> 02:44.796
MAN: Sure is.

02:44.921 --> 02:46.297
My name's Dock.

02:46.422 --> 02:47.882
Mind if I ask who you are?

02:48.007 --> 02:52.053
We're, um, from the Earth
Kingdom colonies.

02:52.178 --> 02:54.013
DOCK: Wow, colonials.

02:54.347 --> 02:56.724
Hop on, I'll give you a ride
into town.

02:59.435 --> 03:01.479
KATARA: Why do you guys
live on the river?

03:01.604 --> 03:03.481
Because we're a fishing town.

03:03.606 --> 03:06.317
At least that's how it was
before the factory moved in.

03:06.442 --> 03:09.070
Army makes their metal there.

03:09.195 --> 03:12.365
Moved in a few years ago and
started gunking up our river.

03:12.490 --> 03:15.284
Now our little village is
struggling to survive.

03:21.290 --> 03:24.919
AANG: Thanks for the ride.

03:25.044 --> 03:27.255
KATARA: Look at this place.

03:27.380 --> 03:29.006
It's so sad.

03:29.132 --> 03:32.009
We have to do something to help.

03:32.135 --> 03:34.595
No, we can't waste
our time here.

03:34.721 --> 03:37.306
We have a bigger mission
that we need to stay focused on.

03:37.432 --> 03:39.726
These people are on their own.

03:39.851 --> 03:43.479
These people are starving,
but you turn your back on them?

03:43.604 --> 03:46.149
How can you be so cold
and heartless?

03:46.274 --> 03:49.318
I'm not turning my back,
I'm just being realistic.

03:49.444 --> 03:52.488
We can't go around helping every
rinky-dink town we wander into.

03:52.613 --> 03:55.283
We'll be helping them all
by taking out the Fire Lord.

03:55.408 --> 03:56.909
TOPH: Hey, loudmouth...

03:57.034 --> 03:59.120
Maybe we should be
a little quieter

03:59.245 --> 04:02.081
When we talk about taking out
the Fire Lord.

04:02.206 --> 04:04.375
Come on, Katara,
be reasonable about this.

04:04.500 --> 04:06.252
You know our mission
has to come first.

04:06.377 --> 04:08.796
I guess so.

04:08.921 --> 04:10.423
Let's just get
what we need and go.

04:17.221 --> 04:19.390
( BELL RINGS )
Hey, Dock, you work here too?

04:19.515 --> 04:21.934
I'm not Dock, I'm Shoe.

04:22.059 --> 04:24.020
Dock's my brother.

04:24.145 --> 04:25.646
But we just saw you.

04:25.772 --> 04:27.774
You're even wearing
the same clothes.

04:27.899 --> 04:29.859
The only difference is your hat.

04:29.984 --> 04:33.154
Dock works on the Docks,
that's why they call him "Dock."

04:33.279 --> 04:36.199
And I work in the shop,
that's why they call me "Shoe."

04:36.324 --> 04:37.492
I don't get it.

04:37.617 --> 04:40.203
Me neither.

04:40.328 --> 04:42.246
What can I get you?

04:42.371 --> 04:43.498
( FLIES BUZZING )

04:43.623 --> 04:45.625
Hey, I'll give you
a special deal.

04:45.750 --> 04:50.505
If you buy three fish,
I'll throw in a clam for free.

04:50.630 --> 04:52.423
( SQUISH )

04:52.548 --> 04:55.843
-( BOTH GROAN )
- We'll just take the fish.

04:55.968 --> 04:59.722
Mind telling your brother
we need a ride back to shore?

04:59.847 --> 05:01.432
Hey, colonials.

05:01.557 --> 05:03.559
My brother says you need a lift.

05:07.480 --> 05:10.107
Can you spare some food?

05:10.233 --> 05:13.152
I wish I could help more.

05:25.206 --> 05:29.669
( WATER SPLASHING )

05:29.794 --> 05:32.964
Our detour into town today
has completely thrown off our schedule.

05:33.089 --> 05:37.093
It's gonna take some serious
finagling to get us back on track.

05:37.218 --> 05:40.513
Finagle away,
o schedule master.

05:40.638 --> 05:41.681
Well, for starters, it looks like we'll

05:41.764 --> 05:43.724
need to wake up 43 minutes earlier
every day.

05:43.850 --> 05:45.935
KATARA: 43 minutes?

05:46.060 --> 05:48.062
Look, we only have a few weeks to get to

05:48.145 --> 05:50.565
the Fire Lord in time for the invasion
and the eclipse

05:50.690 --> 05:52.692
which, by the way,
only lasts for eight minutes.

05:52.817 --> 05:54.610
And we just lost a whole day.

05:54.735 --> 05:57.405
So if we want to make up
the time and stay on schedule

05:57.530 --> 05:58.823
we have to wake up early.

05:58.948 --> 06:01.284
Well, I'm not
waking up early.

06:01.409 --> 06:04.453
Or we could just cut out
all of our eating breaks.

06:04.579 --> 06:06.414
- What?
- No way. Forget it.

06:06.539 --> 06:08.708
I got it, how's this?

06:08.833 --> 06:11.502
From now on, we'll take
food breaks and potty breaks

06:11.627 --> 06:13.045
at the same time.

06:13.170 --> 06:14.380
Ew.

06:14.505 --> 06:16.757
Hey, it might be gross,
but it's efficient.

06:16.883 --> 06:19.552
Either way, we have to
leave here first thing tomorrow morning.

06:25.683 --> 06:28.144
( APPA GROANING )

06:28.269 --> 06:29.353
What's the matter, Katara?

06:29.478 --> 06:31.397
I think Appa's sick.

06:31.522 --> 06:34.066
What, Appa's sick?
That's awful.

06:34.191 --> 06:37.528
TOPH: Wow, Sokka, I didn't
realize you cared so much.

06:37.653 --> 06:39.322
Of course I care.

06:39.447 --> 06:44.493
I might as well just
throw our schedule away now.

06:44.619 --> 06:49.040
And I'm concerned because my
big, furry friend doesn't feel well.

06:49.165 --> 06:50.499
TOPH: He must've gotten sick

06:50.625 --> 06:52.251
from being in the
polluted water.

06:52.376 --> 06:53.586
AANG: He doesn't look sick.

06:53.711 --> 06:55.379
Are you OK, buddy?

06:55.504 --> 06:57.506
( GROANS )

06:57.632 --> 06:59.175
His tongue is purple.

06:59.300 --> 07:00.676
That can't be good.

07:00.801 --> 07:02.386
Katara, can you heal him?

07:02.511 --> 07:04.430
It looks like he needs
some medicine.

07:04.555 --> 07:07.850
Maybe we can find
the right herbs in town.

07:11.479 --> 07:15.232
TOPH: Is it just me, or
does this place seem different?

07:15.358 --> 07:18.027
AANG: Yeah,
are the people happier?

07:18.152 --> 07:23.532
( CHILD LAUGHING )

07:23.658 --> 07:26.035
SOKKA: Hey, Shoe, what's
going on with everyone today?

07:26.160 --> 07:29.997
Ah, something amazing happened
last night.

07:30.122 --> 07:34.210
Food was delivered to our village by
a mysterious and wonderful person.

07:34.335 --> 07:36.504
The Painted Lady.

07:36.629 --> 07:37.630
The painted who now?

07:37.713 --> 07:39.590
The Painted Lady.

07:39.715 --> 07:41.884
She's part of our town's lore.

07:42.009 --> 07:43.678
They say she's a river spirit

07:43.803 --> 07:46.597
who watches over our town
in times of need.

07:46.722 --> 07:48.474
I always thought she was
just a legend.

07:48.599 --> 07:51.060
Until now.

07:51.185 --> 07:52.728
SOKKA: See, we don't need to help
these people,

07:52.812 --> 07:54.730
they already have someone to help them.

07:54.855 --> 07:57.274
All we need is medicine
for our sick friend.

07:57.400 --> 07:58.651
SHOE: Medicine?

07:58.776 --> 08:02.113
Sorry, all the medicine we have
goes to the factory.

08:02.238 --> 08:05.241
That's why there's so many
sick people in our village.

08:05.366 --> 08:08.119
Looks like we need to stay
another night so Appa can rest.

08:08.244 --> 08:10.329
( SIGHS ) I guess you're right.

08:10.454 --> 08:12.915
You got any more food to sell?

08:13.040 --> 08:16.544
Would you like the one-headed
fish or the two-headed fish?

08:16.669 --> 08:19.630
Two-headed.

08:19.755 --> 08:22.174
What, you get more
for your money that way.

08:22.299 --> 08:23.551
( ALL GROAN )

08:23.676 --> 08:25.678
( FLIES BUZZING )

08:32.643 --> 08:34.645
( ♪... )

09:03.090 --> 09:06.594
Thank you, Painted Lady.

09:06.719 --> 09:09.513
( WATER SPLASHES )

09:18.272 --> 09:20.316
Hi, Dock, is Shoe around?

09:20.441 --> 09:24.945
Let me check... ( WHISTLING )

09:25.071 --> 09:27.656
( WHISTLING ) Hey there,
back again, are you?

09:27.782 --> 09:29.408
We need more food.

09:29.533 --> 09:33.412
Our friend is still sick and we
can't leave until he's better.

09:33.537 --> 09:35.456
Oh, well,
that's too bad.

09:35.581 --> 09:37.166
Maybe if you guys are lucky

09:37.291 --> 09:39.210
the Painted Lady will
visit you in the night

09:39.335 --> 09:40.419
and heal your friend.

09:40.544 --> 09:42.880
And maybe she'll cook us
a midnight snack

09:43.005 --> 09:44.465
and we'll all have a sing-along.

09:44.590 --> 09:46.926
Yeah, maybe.

09:47.051 --> 09:49.261
You know, last night
she visited us again.

09:49.386 --> 09:51.472
Healed most of our sick folks.

09:51.597 --> 09:53.557
AANG: Is that why this place
seems so festive?

09:53.682 --> 09:57.144
SHOE: Yep, it's all because of
the Painted Lady.

09:57.269 --> 10:01.315
KATARA: Can you believe how much an entire
village can be affected by one lady?

10:01.440 --> 10:02.983
I mean, spirit?

10:03.109 --> 10:04.735
Well, I hope she returns
every night.

10:04.860 --> 10:07.446
Otherwise this place would go
right back to the way it was.

10:07.530 --> 10:09.240
Why would you say that?

10:09.323 --> 10:11.158
Look how much better off
these people are.

10:11.242 --> 10:14.245
Yeah, now, but without her, they wouldn't
be able to fend for themselves.

10:14.495 --> 10:16.580
If she really wanted to help

10:16.705 --> 10:19.500
she would use her spirit magic
to blow up that factory.

10:19.625 --> 10:23.546
Ooh... ( IMITATES EXPLOSION )

10:23.671 --> 10:26.006
Spirit magic doesn't work
that way, Sokka.

10:26.132 --> 10:31.595
It's more like...
Whoo... ( IMITATES EXPLOSION )

10:31.720 --> 10:34.473
-( LAUGHING )
- Whoo...

11:00.291 --> 11:04.628
( MOMO CHATTERING )

11:04.753 --> 11:07.298
What's the matter, buddy?

11:07.423 --> 11:10.509
It's her.

11:10.634 --> 11:12.178
Hello, Painted Lady spirit.

11:21.645 --> 11:24.607
Excuse me,
I don't mean to bother you

11:24.732 --> 11:28.402
but my friend's sick and we're
on kind of a tight schedule.

11:28.485 --> 11:32.615
Wait, but I'm the great bridge
between your world and mine.

11:32.865 --> 11:38.037
( ICE CRACKLING )

11:39.038 --> 11:41.916
AANG: I know Hei Bai,
we're close personal friends.

11:54.053 --> 11:55.512
Hey.

11:55.638 --> 11:57.640
( GRUNTS )

12:01.393 --> 12:06.690
( PANTING )

12:06.774 --> 12:08.859
( GASPS )

12:08.943 --> 12:09.944
My name's Aang.

12:10.027 --> 12:13.113
I'm the Avatar.

12:13.197 --> 12:15.491
Well, hello, Avatar.

12:15.574 --> 12:18.869
I wish I could talk,
but I am very busy.

12:19.161 --> 12:20.496
Yeah, me too.

12:20.579 --> 12:23.332
I hate that.

12:23.415 --> 12:25.751
You know, you're really pretty
for a spirit.

12:25.834 --> 12:27.419
I don't get to meet too many spirits,

12:27.503 --> 12:30.297
but the ones I do meet...
Not very attractive.

12:30.839 --> 12:33.259
( CHUCKLES ) Thank you, but...

12:33.384 --> 12:36.262
You seem familiar, too.

12:36.387 --> 12:38.055
A lot of people say that.

12:38.180 --> 12:41.016
No, you really seem familiar.

12:41.141 --> 12:45.104
Look, I really should
get going.

12:48.774 --> 12:51.026
Katara?

12:51.151 --> 12:52.403
Hi, Aang.

12:52.528 --> 12:55.239
You're the Painted Lady?
But how?

12:55.364 --> 12:58.659
I wasn't at first, I was just
trying to help the village.

12:58.784 --> 13:00.995
But since everyone thought
that's who I was anyway...

13:01.120 --> 13:05.916
I guess I just kind of
became her.

13:06.041 --> 13:08.252
So you've been sneaking out
at night?

13:08.377 --> 13:10.713
Wait, is Appa even sick?

13:10.838 --> 13:14.425
He might be sick of the purple
berries I've been feeding him

13:14.550 --> 13:16.677
but other than that, he's fine.

13:16.802 --> 13:19.722
I can't believe you lied to
everyone so you could help these people.

13:19.847 --> 13:22.141
I'm sorry,
I know I shouldn't have.

13:22.266 --> 13:23.684
No, I think it's great.

13:23.809 --> 13:26.562
You're like a secret hero.

13:26.687 --> 13:28.647
Well, if you want to help...

13:28.772 --> 13:32.109
There's one more thing
I have to do.

13:41.035 --> 13:43.370
You want to destroy
this factory?

13:43.454 --> 13:46.540
Yes, Sokka was just kidding,
but he was right.

13:46.623 --> 13:50.127
Getting rid of this factory is the only
way to help these people permanently.

14:14.735 --> 14:16.695
( ♪... )

14:43.514 --> 14:44.973
Ha-ha...
( IMITATES EXPLOSION )

14:45.057 --> 14:48.477
Shh, we don't want to
wake Sokka.

14:48.811 --> 14:50.646
Hi... Sokka.

14:50.896 --> 14:53.649
We were just out
on a morning walk.

14:53.941 --> 14:55.067
Oh, really?

14:55.275 --> 14:58.487
A morning walk?

15:01.782 --> 15:03.367
I know you're the Painted Lady.

15:03.492 --> 15:05.369
I know you've been sneaking out
at night.

15:05.494 --> 15:07.287
And I know you've been lying about Appa

15:07.371 --> 15:09.873
and feeding him
purple-izing-tongue berries.

15:09.998 --> 15:12.751
- Ah.
-( MOMO CHATTERS )

15:12.876 --> 15:15.212
Katara, what you did put our
whole mission in jeopardy.

15:15.337 --> 15:19.842
We're leaving right now.

15:19.967 --> 15:22.052
And how long did you
know about this?

15:22.177 --> 15:24.972
Hey, I just found out
this morning.

15:46.243 --> 15:47.870
What's going on?

15:47.995 --> 15:50.080
Fire Nation soldiers are
heading to the village.

15:50.205 --> 15:51.790
What did you do?

15:51.915 --> 15:53.792
I kind of destroyed
their factory.

15:53.917 --> 15:55.043
You what?

15:55.169 --> 15:58.005
- It was your idea.
- I was joking.

15:58.130 --> 16:01.341
I also said to use spirit magic
and made funny noises.

16:01.467 --> 16:03.886
( GROANS ) Did you even
think this through?

16:04.011 --> 16:05.804
The army's gonna blame
the villagers.

16:05.929 --> 16:07.806
They're headed there right now
to get revenge.

16:07.931 --> 16:09.558
Well, what was I supposed to do?

16:09.683 --> 16:11.351
Leave, do nothing.

16:12.686 --> 16:13.687
No.

16:13.770 --> 16:16.982
I will never, ever turn my back
on people who need me.

16:17.483 --> 16:20.027
I'm going down to the village

16:20.110 --> 16:23.030
And I am gonna do
whatever I can.

16:27.034 --> 16:28.076
Wait.

16:28.202 --> 16:30.329
I'm coming too.

16:30.454 --> 16:32.581
I thought you didn't
want to help.

16:32.706 --> 16:36.210
You need me, and I will never
turn my back on you.

16:36.335 --> 16:40.756
Sokka, you really do have
a heart.

16:40.881 --> 16:44.468
He really does have a heart,
doesn't he?

16:44.593 --> 16:45.886
( GRUNTS )

16:46.011 --> 16:48.263
( ♪... )

16:54.561 --> 16:57.022
( ♪... )

16:57.147 --> 16:59.566
I thought we could live
as neighbors in peace

16:59.691 --> 17:01.235
but I guess I was wrong.

17:01.360 --> 17:03.987
You steal our food,
our medicine...

17:04.112 --> 17:06.198
And then you destroy
our factory.

17:06.323 --> 17:08.742
We didn't do any of that.

17:08.867 --> 17:11.745
Yeah, the Painted Lady
brought us food.

17:11.870 --> 17:14.623
She's the one that healed
our sick, not your medicine.

17:14.748 --> 17:19.586
Oh, right, the mysterious
Painted Lady did it.

17:19.711 --> 17:24.716
And I suppose she drew the army
emblem on your containers, too.

17:24.841 --> 17:26.260
( CROWD GASPS )

17:26.385 --> 17:29.805
This is a town of thieves
and liars.

17:29.930 --> 17:32.891
( GRUNTS )

17:33.016 --> 17:37.646
Where's your Painted Lady now?

17:37.771 --> 17:40.524
We're going to cure the world
of this wretched village.

18:00.836 --> 18:04.673
Light it again.

18:04.798 --> 18:07.593
Look at that,
where's it coming from?

18:07.718 --> 18:09.261
I don't know.

18:09.386 --> 18:11.638
Something strange is going on.

18:11.763 --> 18:13.890
( DISTANT ROARING )

18:14.016 --> 18:15.684
( WHISPERS )
It's the Painted Lady.

18:15.809 --> 18:17.644
( SINGSONG ) She's coming.

18:17.769 --> 18:19.605
There is no Painted Lady.

18:19.730 --> 18:23.358
( ROARING AND LOUD THUDS )

18:33.327 --> 18:35.579
( PLAYING EERIE TUNE )

18:39.833 --> 18:42.753
- What is that sound?
- Maybe it is her.

19:00.103 --> 19:01.938
Do something.

19:07.027 --> 19:08.820
( BOTH SCREAM )

19:13.450 --> 19:16.119
Stand your ground.

19:36.932 --> 19:39.184
I'll take care of you myself.

19:45.315 --> 19:46.316
( GRUNTS )

19:59.913 --> 20:00.997
( SCREAMS )

20:01.081 --> 20:04.751
( GRUNTING )

20:04.876 --> 20:06.920
( GASPING )

20:10.590 --> 20:13.552
Leave this village
and never come back.

20:27.941 --> 20:31.027
( DISTANT CHEERING AND WHISTLING )

20:36.867 --> 20:39.745
( CHEERING )

20:43.039 --> 20:44.791
I knew you'd come.

20:44.916 --> 20:46.251
DOCK: Thank you.

20:46.376 --> 20:48.086
MAN: Painted Lady,
you're the best.

20:48.211 --> 20:51.923
Me and my brothers
really owe you a lot.

20:52.048 --> 20:55.886
Hey, wait a minute,
I know you.

20:56.011 --> 20:58.096
You're not the Painted Lady.

20:58.221 --> 21:01.099
You're that colonial girl.

21:01.224 --> 21:04.811
Yeah, you're the lady
that gave me a fish.

21:04.936 --> 21:06.813
You've been tricking us.

21:06.938 --> 21:09.191
You're a waterbender.

21:09.316 --> 21:10.901
She's a waterbender.

21:11.026 --> 21:13.236
MAN: How dare you act like
our Painted Lady?

21:13.361 --> 21:16.072
( CROWD GRUMBLING )

21:16.198 --> 21:19.701
Maybe she is a waterbender, but
she was just trying to help you.

21:19.826 --> 21:22.412
Because of her, that factory
won't be polluting your river

21:22.537 --> 21:24.206
and the army is gone.

21:24.331 --> 21:26.750
You should be down on your knees
thanking her.

21:26.875 --> 21:29.836
Sokka, it's OK.

21:29.961 --> 21:32.130
I shouldn't have acted like
someone I wasn't

21:32.255 --> 21:33.965
and I shouldn't have
tricked you.

21:34.090 --> 21:36.802
But I felt like I had to
do something.

21:36.927 --> 21:40.013
It doesn't matter if
the Painted Lady is real or not.

21:40.138 --> 21:43.934
Because your problems are real,
and this river is real.

21:44.059 --> 21:46.561
You can't wait around
for someone to help you.

21:46.686 --> 21:48.897
You have to help yourself.

21:49.022 --> 21:52.567
She's right,
but what should we do?

21:52.692 --> 21:55.821
Maybe we can clean
the river.

21:55.946 --> 21:59.074
Yeah, we can clean the river.

21:59.199 --> 22:02.828
( CROWD CHEERING )

22:02.953 --> 22:04.538
DOCK: Thank you.

22:04.663 --> 22:07.707
You know, you're not so bad
for a waterbender.

22:07.833 --> 22:10.252
You wouldn't mind keeping that
a secret, by the way, would you?

22:10.377 --> 22:12.003
No problem.

22:12.128 --> 22:14.381
Keeping my mouth shut is
a personal specialty.

22:14.506 --> 22:17.759
My brother Shoe, on the other
hand, ho, he's a blabbermouth.

22:17.884 --> 22:19.094
( GROANS )

22:19.219 --> 22:21.388
So, Dock, are you gonna
help us clean?

22:21.513 --> 22:24.808
No, ma'am, I'm going to get
my other brother, Bushi.

22:24.933 --> 22:29.062
He loves cleaning rivers.

22:29.187 --> 22:30.897
All right, I'm Bushi.

22:31.022 --> 22:32.899
Let's get some
river cleaning done.

22:33.024 --> 22:35.151
Aha, I knew it.

22:35.277 --> 22:37.028
I knew you were the same guy.

22:37.153 --> 22:39.739
You're the shop owner
and the boat guy.

22:39.865 --> 22:42.826
Oh, you must be talking about
my brothers, Dock and Shoe.

22:42.951 --> 22:44.744
No, I just saw you.

22:44.870 --> 22:46.830
You switched hats and called
yourself a different name.

22:46.955 --> 22:49.207
Oh, you know who does that?

22:49.332 --> 22:51.418
My brother Dock.

22:51.543 --> 22:53.253
He's crazy.

22:53.378 --> 22:56.840
( LAUGHS )

23:06.558 --> 23:09.060
( WATER SPLASHING )

23:33.084 --> 23:35.921
Thank you.

23:50.060 --> 23:53.730
( ♪... )
